; -- IKEMEN GO DOJO MODULE -------------------------------------------------
; ---- dojo.def - graphic elements / UI configuration for every mode the
; ---- Dojo hosts: Trials, the Game Tutorial and Character Guides.
; ---- Loaded by dojo.lua, not by the screenpack's system.def, so it is not
; ---- part of the main menu or pause menu. The settings provided in this
; ---- file are defaults that show an integration with the `ikemen1`
; ---- screenpack.
; --
; ---- Three sections:
; ----   Dojo           - the look every mode shares. Restyle here once.
; ----   Trials Mode    - laid over it for Trials.
; ----   Tutorial Mode  - laid over it for the Game Tutorial and Character
; ----                    Guides.
; ---- The two mode sections only need the keys that differ; shipped, that
; ---- is their labels ("Trial" vs "Lesson"). Any key from the Dojo section
; ---- can be repeated in either one to style that mode apart.
; --
; ---- Key names are mode-neutral (title, steps, counter, menu, ...).
; ---- The older spellings are still read, in any section: Trials Mode's
; ---- (trialtitle, trialsteps, trialcounter, trialsmenu, ...) and the old
; ---- standalone tutorialmode.def's (lessontitle, lessonsteps,
; ---- lessoncounter, tutorialmenu, ...), so a section copied from either
; ---- still works. A trialsmode.def from Trials Mode 1.x, which has no Dojo
; ---- section, can be dropped in as dojo.def: its Trials Mode section is
; ---- then used as the shared look.
; --
; -- Module developed by two4teezee
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------

[Dojo]
; NOTE: Values provided in this sample meant for `ikemen1` screenpack, 1280x720 resolution.
; Please modify the values in this file to properly configure the modes for your screenpack.
; Throughout, "trial" stands for any exercise, a trial or a lesson alike: the modes share one engine.
; The on-screen labels (titles, counters, timers, the list title) are in [Trials Mode] and
; [Tutorial Mode] at the end of this file.

; GENERAL OPTIONS ----------------------------------------------------------
; localcoord: localcoord for the modes' UI. Defaults to 320,240 if not specified.
; listdisplay: valid values are "select", "start", and "off". "select" shows the menu between stage select and the fight loading; "start" shows it once the match is up, over the frozen pair; "off" never asks and starts on the first trial. Defaults to "start". The pause menu's list works the same either way. The Game Tutorial always picks its lesson from its own list before the match.
; --   Note: "select" falls back to the "start" menu for characters whose trials use showforvarvalpairs. Those trials are picked by the player's groove or mode, and the variables holding it do not exist until the match is up, so asking before the fight would list every groove's trials.
; --
; Layout (vertical/horizontal) and Reset on Success are player preferences, not UI config. Their
; shipped defaults and the player's saved choices both live in config.ini's [Options] - see the
; legend at the top of that file. Layout also selects the scrolling behaviour and enables dynamic
; step width; the fadein/fadeout parameters below still style the Reset on Success transition.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
localcoord = 1280,720
listdisplay = select

; ELEMENT ANCHORS ----------------------------------------------------------
; Everything below is authored on the localcoord canvas, but the screen it lands on is
; whatever aspect the match is running at. With the aspect ratio option set to "stage", every
; stage can bring its own, so a UI authored at 1280,720 has to survive a 4:3 stage.
;
; The module keeps the authored scale - text and sprites are the same size at every aspect - and
; moves each element to the edge it was authored against. "anchor" is which edge that is:
;   left   - keeps its distance from the left edge (the default for anything authored on the left)
;   center - stays the same fraction across
;   right  - keeps its distance from the right edge
; The elements that take it are title.<layout>, steps.<layout>, counter,
; totaltimer, currenttimer, reset.text, textbox, success, allclear and menu.
; Leave it out and the module infers one from where the element sits on the canvas, which is right
; for the usual corner-pinned HUD but is only a guess - say it outright if the element matters.
;
; The two windows authored in canvas space - steps.<layout>.window.* and
; menu.overlay.window - are not anchored: each edge follows its own side of the screen, so
; they keep their authored margins and stretch or narrow with the aspect.
;
; None of this does anything when the stage's aspect matches the canvas: every number below is
; then used exactly as authored.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; BACKGROUND ELEMENT LAYERS ------------------------------------------------
; Every bg and front element below (including the horizontal layout's bg.tail and bg.head)
; accepts a "layerno" parameter. Valid values are -1, 0, 1 and 2; anything higher is clamped
; to 2. Defaults to 0, which is where every trials element used to be drawn.
; All of these layers are drawn on top of the stage and the characters - layerno only orders
; trials elements against each other. Elements sharing a layer keep their usual draw order
; (steps bg, trial title, textbox, then the individual steps and their glyphs), so
; raising an element's layerno is how you pull it in front of something that would normally
; be drawn after it.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; WHERE SPRITES AND SOUNDS COME FROM ---------------------------------------
; Every "spr" and "anim" below is resolved out of the module's own dojo.sff when one sits
; beside dojo.lua, and out of the screenpack's system.sff when it does not.
; Sounds work the same way: every "snd" parameter in this file (success.snd, allclear.snd) is
; resolved out of an optional dojo.snd beside dojo.lua, and out of the screenpack's
; system.snd when there is none. The module ships a dojo.sff but no dojo.snd, so sounds
; come from the screenpack out of the box - drop a dojo.snd in and they come from it instead.
; It is the whole file that switches, not one sound at a time: once a dojo.snd is present,
; a group,number missing from it plays nothing rather than falling back to system.snd.
; The pause menu's own sounds are not affected either way. cursor.move, cursor.done, enter and
; cancel are read from the screenpack's [Trials Pause Menu] / [Tutorial Pause Menu] / [Pause Menu] section and always
; play out of system.snd, so the list answers like every other menu in the screenpack.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; SELSCREENPALFX -----------------------------------------------------------
; Sets specified palfx color to character portraits WITHOUT trials files in the trials select screen. See definition for palfx for different fields and options.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
selscreenpalfx.color = 0
selscreenpalfx.invertall = ; 0
selscreenpalfx.sinadd = ; 0, 0, 0, 0
selscreenpalfx.mul = 100, 100, 100
selscreenpalfx.add = ; 0, 0, 0

; RESETONSUCCESS FADES -----------------------------------------------------
; Used when Reset on Success is enabled (config.ini [Options] Trials.ResetOnSuccess / Tutorial.ResetOnSuccess = true).
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
fadein.time = 40
fadein.col = {0, 0, 0}
fadein.anim = -1
fadeout.time = 40
fadeout.col = {0, 0, 0}
fadeout.anim = -1

